.SH NAME
logout \- terminate the current login session
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B logout
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Logout
terminates a login shell.
Especially useful if
.I ignoreeof
is set.
.SH LIMITATIONS
\fBLogout\fR will only execute from the \fIlogin\fR shell.
.sp
the \fIlogout\fR process does not recognize interupts
.SH SEE ALSO
exit(1C), kill(1), onintr(1C).
.br
\fIThe C Shell\fR in the ZEUS Utilities Manual
